<section class="full" aria-label="Case study">
  <div class="card">

    <div class="callout">
      A single source of truth for recruiting assets — reducing duplicate effort, accelerating social promotion, and making employer branding wins usable in every candidate conversation.
    </div>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="Context">
      <h2 class="section-title">Context</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Recruiters relied on scattered documents, Slack threads, email attachments, and outdated shared drives
        to locate candidate materials, employer branding collateral, and social promotion content.
        Information existed — but it was fragmented and difficult to access quickly.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Recruiters often recreated materials, used outdated links, or delayed outreach while searching
        for the correct assets. The system worked — but it was inefficient and inconsistent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="The constraint">
      <h2 class="section-title">The Constraint</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Without a structured repository, execution speed depended on memory and personal file organization
        rather than shared infrastructure.
      </p>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Candidate-facing materials were inconsistently routed</li>
        <li>Recruiters spent unnecessary time locating links and documents</li>
        <li>Social media promotion required manual coordination each time</li>
        <li>Employee referral campaigns lacked centralized assets</li>
        <li>Employer branding wins — including Best Places to Work recognition — were under-leveraged</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="What we did">
      <h2 class="section-title">What We Did</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        I designed and implemented a centralized document management repository organized into
        structured, accessible categories — prioritizing ease of access, version control clarity,
        and logical categorization to reduce friction during live recruiting workflows.
      </p>

      <h3>Candidate Materials</h3>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Interview prep guides and role-specific collateral</li>
        <li>Take-home instructions and onboarding handoff documentation</li>
        <li>Centralized routing links for consistent candidate access</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Employer Branding & Social Promotion</h3>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Best Places to Work badges and announcement assets</li>
        <li>Job posting promotion templates and pre-written social media captions</li>
        <li>Referral request campaigns and outreach messaging templates</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Recruiter Enablement Tools</h3>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Standardized email templates and approved candidate communications</li>
        <li>Easy-to-copy promotional snippets for social and referral outreach</li>
        <li>Updated referral incentives and process guides</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="Impact">
      <h2 class="section-title">Impact</h2>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Recruiters accessed approved materials instantly rather than recreating content</li>
        <li>Social promotion and referral outreach became easier to execute consistently</li>
        <li>Employer branding recognition was leveraged in candidate conversations rather than sitting unused</li>
        <li>Candidate materials were routed more reliably and professionally</li>
        <li>Duplicate effort and informal asset recreation were reduced</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout">
        The recruiting team operated from a shared, up-to-date information layer rather than fragmented personal systems.
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="Why it matters">
      <h2 class="section-title">Why It Matters</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Recruiting performance is influenced not just by sourcing volume or interview quality,
        but by operational enablement. When recruiting assets are centralized and structured,
        execution speed increases, messaging consistency improves, brand positioning strengthens,
        and team variability decreases.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Infrastructure clarity supports recruiter confidence and candidate trust.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</section>
